# Input
```css
/* should not generate diagnostics */

/* Each `&` contributes the parent specificity, so `& & .c` is more specific than `& .c` */
.a {
  & .c {}
  & & .c {}
}

/* The `&` refers to the nearest parent, whose specificity includes its ancestors */
.x {
  .y {
    & .d {}
    html body & .d {}
  }
}

```
